auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Rating the food, from the diner's side. Requires `X-Guest-Token`.

  **Sequenced last on purpose.** The rating window does not open until the food has reached the
  table, and in a sequential run that does not happen until `admin-orders / mark-served`. Placing
  this folder before that one would assert against a closed window and fail for a reason that has
  nothing to do with the endpoint.

  The window itself is deliberately not "status is served". It opens on whichever of several
  signals fires first -- staff marking the order served, a counter payment settling, or a timeout
  after the kitchen stopped updating the order at all. Tying it to the served tap alone would mean
  every diner at a restaurant whose floor staff stop tapping mid-service is never asked to rate.
  `backend/internal/services/review_window.go` is the single authority.
}
